  "body": "Stacked on #1539 (merge it first). Branched from #1539 (stacked); contains #1539 at 47704e3a.\n\n## What changed\n- **New `camcraft_app::stock_fit`** (84 lines): `part_bounds` (the #1529 `part_aabb_in` set: every model but the fixtures), `part_radius_about_in` (its parts-only radius twin for the snug cylinder), `fitted` and `fit_command` - the one undoable `SetStock` for the box, cylinder and per-side fits, the stock's rotation kept, refusals by name (same wording as before).\n- **GUI**: `State`'s `StockFit` / `StockFitSides` and `apply_stock_fit` now call `stock_fit::fit_command` (the fit logic left the UI layer; `state.rs` -48 lines). The Stock page's \"Models: ...\" strip (`stock_info.rs`) reads `stock_fit::part_bounds`.\n- **WCS pane** (coordinator's request): the \"model bounds\" anchor source (`interact::anchor_reference`) reads the same parts-only box, so G54 set from model bounds lands on the part's corner, not the vise's.\n- **MCP**: new tool `fit_stock` (`crates/app/src/mcp/stock_fit_tools.rs`) - `shape` box/cylinder with `margin`, or `sides` [-X,+X,-Y,+Y,-Z,+Z]. Same command as the GUI, one History step. There was no MCP or script fit before (`set_stock` takes explicit sizes only).\n- Collision checks untouched: fixtures are still judged by every collision law.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1538-fit-stock-excludes-fixtures.md`.\n\n## Pins (each mutation-checked)\n| Pin | Mutation | Red | Restored |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `stock_fit_fixtures::fit_box_with_a_vise_wraps_the_part_plus_the_margin` (50x50x6 part + 5 in vise -> Box 54x54x10 at 0.5..54.5, Z 2..12) | `part_bounds` back to `solid_aabb_in` | FAILED | ok |\n| `stock_fit_fixtures::fit_cylinder_with_a_vise_is_snug_about_the_part` (d = 2(25 sqrt2 + 2)) | `solid_aabb_in`; and separately the radius keeps fixtures | FAILED both | ok |\n| `stock_fit_fixtures::every_fixture_kind_is_left_out_of_every_fit` (vise, soft jaw, plate, tagged clamp; box/cylinder/sides equal the bare part's) | both mutations | FAILED both | ok |\n| `stock_fit_fixtures::mcp_fit_stock_with_a_vise_gives_the_part_box` (MCP import, set_stock, add_builtin_vise fit_to_stock, fit_stock box/cylinder/sides, bad shape refused, undo) | both mutations | FAILED both | ok |\n| `shell::stock_fit_with_a_vise_wraps_the_part_not_the_vise` (GUI `CommandKind::StockFit` box and cylinder through `State`) | both mutations | FAILED both | ok |\n| `egui_app::stock_info::tests::the_readout_is_the_parts_never_the_vise` (\"Models: 50.000 x 50.000 x 6.000 mm\") | `solid_aabb_in` | FAILED | ok |\n| `egui_app::setup_align_tests::model_bounds_anchors_are_the_parts_never_the_vise` (SW/NE/C anchors on the part; SetWcs from SW puts G54 at (2.5, 2.5, 4)) | `anchor_reference` back to `solid_aabb_in` | FAILED | ok |\n\nAlso: `the_fit_is_one_undoable_step`, `fixtures_alone_are_nothing_to_fit_and_a_bad_side_is_refused`.\n\n## Gates\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head b3612bde: ok (app suites 50 s incl. stock_fit_fixtures, heights_fixtures, mcp, every mcp_* suite; ui suites 27 s incl. shell, fixtures, lib).\n- ui lib single-threaded from `crates/ui`: 712 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored.\n- Stock suites: stock_fit_fixtures 6, heights_fixtures 5, setup_stock_source 8, setup_stock_view 3, stock_view 4, stock_source_verdict 22, mcp 22 - all ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- #1539 had not moved past b3107a5f when this opened (merge of `origin/issue/1529-heights-exclude-fixtures`: already up to date).\n\n## Not exercised\n- The live GUI (no window opened); the GUI path is driven through `State` and the strip through its line builder.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill's tool table does not list `fit_stock` yet: it is a process file (`.claude/skills/`), left for a process PR rather than editing it here - skill row: #1552.\n- A `stock_source` \"raw stock only\" model is still measured as a part (same set as #1529's heights); changing that is for both together.\n\nChangelog: Fit to Models (box, cylinder, per-side), the Stock page's model-size readout and the WCS model-bounds anchors measure the parts only, never vises, accessories, plates or tagged fixtures; new MCP tool `fit_stock` (#1538)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1538\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n\n",
